Link against the CUDA driver stub under /opt/cuda as well.

cgo links -lcuda and already searches /usr/local/cuda/lib64/stubs, the
stub's location in NVIDIA's default layout, but for /opt/cuda only
lib64 and lib. Gentoo's nvidia-cuda-toolkit 13 ships libcuda.so only in
/opt/cuda/lib64/stubs, so the link fails on hosts without the driver.
The stub carries the libcuda.so.1 soname, so the real driver still
loads at run time.
--- a/cuda/cu/cgoflags.go
+++ b/cuda/cu/cgoflags.go
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 //#cgo CFLAGS: -I/usr/include
 //
 ////arch linux:
-//#cgo LDFLAGS:-L/opt/cuda/lib64 -L/opt/cuda/lib
+//#cgo LDFLAGS:-L/opt/cuda/lib64 -L/opt/cuda/lib64/stubs -L/opt/cuda/lib
 //#cgo CFLAGS: -I/opt/cuda/include
 //
 ////WINDOWS:
